WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:13.482
Hi! Today we'll learn synonyms and antonyms. Synonyms are words with similar meanings, and antonyms are words with opposite meanings. They make your writing richer, too.

2
00:00:13.632 --> 00:00:20.154
Synonyms: big, huge and enormous all mean large. Enormous is the strongest.

3
00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:28.194
Happy, glad and cheerful all mean pleased. For antonyms, ancient means very old, and its opposite is modern.

4
00:00:28.344 --> 00:00:37.338
Quick, fast and rapid all mean speedy. Brave is the opposite of cowardly, and generous is the opposite of stingy.

5
00:00:37.488 --> 00:00:43.794
Many antonyms are made by adding a prefix. Add un to happy and you get unhappy.

6
00:00:43.944 --> 00:00:47.298
Add dis to honest and you get dishonest.

7
00:00:47.448 --> 00:00:53.730
Add im to possible and you get impossible. Patient becomes impatient in the same way.

8
00:00:53.880 --> 00:01:02.346
Add in to correct and you get incorrect. You have to learn which prefix each word takes, so check a dictionary.

9
00:01:02.496 --> 00:01:10.506
Some words change meaning in different sentences. She is a bright pupil who learns fast. Here bright means clever.

10
00:01:10.656 --> 00:01:19.698
The room is bright and sunny. Here bright means full of light. So always check the sentence when you look for a synonym.

11
00:01:19.848 --> 00:01:25.698
Watch out! Unhonest is wrong. There is no such word in English!

12
00:01:25.848 --> 00:01:30.930
The opposite of honest is dishonest. Not every word takes un.

13
00:01:31.080 --> 00:01:39.594
In the same way, possible becomes impossible, not unpossible. When you're not sure, check a dictionary.

14
00:01:39.744 --> 00:01:52.026
Your turn! The elephant is enormous. Which word is a synonym for enormous: tiny, huge or quick? Pause and think.

15
00:01:52.176 --> 00:02:01.266
The answer is huge. Both mean very big. Tiny is actually its antonym. Did you get it right?

16
00:02:01.416 --> 00:02:11.514
Another one! What is the antonym of ancient: old, modern or famous? Pause and think.

17
00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:19.194
The answer is modern. Old is a synonym, not an antonym. Did you get it right?

18
00:02:19.344 --> 00:02:29.754
Here's another! Patient means able to wait calmly. How do you write its antonym? Pause and think.

19
00:02:29.904 --> 00:02:36.090
The answer is impatient, with the prefix im. Did you get it right?

20
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:48.090
One more! Grandpa is very generous. What is the antonym of generous: kind, stingy or rich? Pause and think.

21
00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:56.874
The answer is stingy. Kind is close in meaning to generous, so it isn't an antonym. Did you get it right?

22
00:02:57.024 --> 00:03:11.250
Remember: synonyms are similar, antonyms are opposite. Many antonyms use the prefixes un, dis, im or in, so learn which one each word takes. And one word can mean different things in different sentences.

23
00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:17.034
In your next composition, try using a more vivid synonym!

